\par }{\i\fs28\lang3081\cgrid0 A.}{\fs28\lang3081\cgrid0  They have come to see us, not to see thee.
\par }{\i\fs28\lang3081\cgrid0 B.}{\fs28\lang3081\cgrid0  May you dream about Elves! (Wish that you will dream about Elves!)}{\b\fs28\lang3081\cgrid0 
\par }{\i\fs28\lang3081\cgrid0 C}{\fs28\lang3081\cgrid0 . Three men will go thither, and the Dwarves will watch them, for the men possess a treasure that is greater than [lit. "great beyond"] gold.
\par }{\i\fs28\lang3081\cgrid0 D.}{\fs28\lang3081\cgrid0  On the sixth day they felt moved to come to me. [Lit. "...(it) impelled for them to come to me."]
\par }{\i\fs28\lang3081\cgrid0 E.}{\fs28\lang3081\cgrid0  The sixth king of the land is wiser than ["wise beyond"] his father the fifth king.}{\i\fs28\lang3081\cgrid0 
\par F.}{\fs28\lang3081\cgrid0  (S)he expanded his/her house, making it [or, that] the biggest house of the street.
\par }{\i\fs28\lang3081\cgrid0 G.}{\fs28\lang3081\cgrid0  You did it for them; you did not do it for us. }{\lang3081\cgrid0 (Alternatively, "you }{\i\lang3081\cgrid0 made}{\lang3081\cgrid0  it for them; you did not }{\i\lang3081\cgrid0 make}{\lang3081\cgrid0 
